  "articleBody": "Starting a shower installation can feel exciting, but it’s super easy to trip up if you’re not careful. One of the biggest blunders we see is poor waterproofing. Seriously, if your waterproofing isn’t spot on, you’re looking at leaks and potential structural damage down the road. It’s not just about slapping on some material; it’s about making sure every seam and corner is sealed perfectly. Another common issue is getting the drainage slope wrong. Your shower pan needs to be angled just right so water actually goes down the drain instead of pooling up. We’ve also seen folks use the wrong drain fittings or completely skip the pan liner, which is a recipe for disaster. And don't even get me started on bad measurements! Thinking you can just eyeball it will often lead to frustrating rework or, worse, a shower that doesn’t fit. Before you know it, you’re dealing with water damage and a bigger headache than you started with. These kinds of mistakes can turn a dream renovation into a nightmare, so it's often best to get a professional involved, especially with the trickier bits like waterproofing and plumbing.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
